<!--Render Target Documentation — Imports
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation.Imports-->
<rdoc:Imports xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:rdoc="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    use and include paths emitted into each SCAD file
  </is>
  <documentation><![CDATA[
    Every generated file imports the MachineBlocks V3 library and the project
    config. Paths are relative to the output file, using mbLibPath from
    targetOptions under the key machineblocks-v3-scad. The compiler
    RenderSession has no mbLibPath field. When mbLibPath is absent this slice
    returns files: [] and diagnostic BML_MB_LIB_PATH_MISSING.

    Standard imports (angle brackets are SCAD include syntax):

        use <{relative_path_to_scad_lib}/lib/block.scad>;
        include <{relative_path_to_scad_lib}/config/mb_config.scad>;

    Ordinary composite compositions render leaf instances as mb_block()
    (NativeBlock). They do not use-import dependency block SCAD files.

    Sets (com.machineblocks.bml.core.Set) reference typed block modules by the
    placed part's type FQN. The set processor emits a use import for each
    distinct type file, for example use <../wall/Wall.scad>, and each instance
    module calls that type's manifestation module.

    When expressions reference a #built-in call that is not a native SCAD
    mapping, the processor adds a use import for that service file, and only
    when the service is actually used:

        use <{relative}/blocks/org/blockml/bml/service/Math.scad>;
        use <{relative}/blocks/org/blockml/bml/service/Strings.scad>;

    Service SCAD files live in @machineblocks/core at
    blocks/org/blockml/bml/service/ (Math.scad, Strings.scad, Numbers.scad,
    Lists.scad, Bools.scad). They are pre-rendered artifacts. BML service
    definitions in @blockml/core are the SSOT. Import paths are always relative
    to the output file directory.
  ]]></documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="rdoc:NativeMappings" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</rdoc:Imports>
